OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CBBC makes power saving by
OL,4,Ckeeping BBC Two off air during daytime
OL,5,
OL,6,FThis was followed by a letter written
OL,7,Fby Mr John Grant, Labour's chief
OL,8,Fspokesman on broadcasting, to the Prime
OL,9,FMinister, Mr Edward Heath, in which he
OL,10,Fcomplained that there had been no
OL,11,Fattempt to explain to the public the
OL,12,Freasons for the restrictions on late
OL,13,Fevening television rather than imposing
OL,14,Fa similar ban during daytime hours.
OL,15,FThis had caused "some surprise in
OL,16,Fbroadcasting circles and some
OL,17,Fbewilderment in the country generally."
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12908
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F129A1768739869
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                  G8/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CBBC makes power saving by
OL,4,Ckeeping BBC Two off air during daytime
OL,5,
OL,6,FMr Grant declared in his letter to the
OL,7,FPrime Minister that there was a
OL,8,Fwidespread belief that the timing of
OL,9,Fthese cuts had been aimed "to create
OL,10,Fmaximum psychological impact as part of
OL,11,Fan overall campaign by the Government
OL,12,Fto turn public opinion against the
OL,13,Ftrade unions even though this may
OL,14,Finvolve an unnecessary degree of
OL,15,Fhardship of discomfort for the
OL,16,Fpublic."The Stage (January 1975)
OL,17,
OL,18,FThe power savingB directly involved
OL,19,Fseemed modest.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100
