OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CBBC makes power saving by
OL,4,Ckeeping BBC Two off air during daytime
OL,5,
OL,6,FNot surprisingly, this restriction was
OL,7,Fvery unpopular with the public as well
OL,8,Fas the broadcasters.
OL,9,
OL,10,FThe election campaign in February 1974
OL,11,Fled to it being lifted. This was
OL,12,Fsupposedly to ensure election
OL,13,Fbroadcasting was not curtailed. It
OL,14,Fsounds suspiciously like a handy cover
OL,15,Fstory.
OL,16,
OL,17,FThe BBC kept on with its voluntary
OL,18,Frestrictions on BBC Two power until the
OL,19,FThree Day Week ended after Labour's
OL,20,Felection victory.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,130,120,200,300,0,100
